{"indicator":"monthly-earnings-ppp","unit":"國際元/月","years":[1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"latestWithin":3,"notes":{"ZAF":"ILOSTAT 2016–2019 年是中位數，不到前後年平均數的一半，所以這幾年不列","BLZ":"ILOSTAT 的 2020 年是中位數，其他國家多半是平均數；少數高薪的人會拉高平均數，所以中位數通常比較低","BMU":"ILOSTAT 的 2012–2013 年是中位數，其他國家多半是平均數；少數高薪的人會拉高平均數，所以中位數通常比較低","HKG":"ILOSTAT 的 2003–2004、2007、2009–2016 年是中位數，其他國家多半是平均數；少數高薪的人會拉高平均數，所以中位數通常比較低","MAC":"ILOSTAT 的 1990–1997、2009–2018 年是中位數，其他國家多半是平均數；少數高薪的人會拉高平均數，所以中位數通常比較低","PAN":"ILOSTAT 的 1998–1999 年是中位數，其他國家多半是平均數；少數高薪的人會拉高平均數，所以中位數通常比較低","SGP":"ILOSTAT 的 2011–2021 年是中位數，其他國家多半是平均數；少數高薪的人會拉高平均數，所以中位數通常比較低","UGA":"ILOSTAT 的 2002、2005 年是中位數，其他國家多半是平均數；少數高薪的人會拉高平均數，所以中位數通常比較低","TWN":"ILOSTAT 沒有台灣（不是國際勞工組織會員），改用主計總處薪資及生產力統計的工業及服務業受僱員工每人每月總薪資（全年平均，含加班費、年終與績效獎金等非經常性薪資；不含農林漁牧業與公共行政），用民間消費的購買力平價換算，跟 ILOSTAT 用的世界銀行 PPP 同一個概念：2021 年以前用 Penn World Table，之後依台灣與美國的消費者物價漲幅往後推（2025 年 1 國際元 = 14.53 新臺幣）。IMF 的 GDP 購買力平價較低（13.65），用它換算會是 4,642 國際元。2025 年總薪資 63,383 元，其中經常性薪資 47,885 元"},"notesEn":{"ZAF":"ILOSTAT's figures for 2016–2019 are medians, less than half the mean reported for the years before and after, so those years are left out","BLZ":"ILOSTAT's figures for 2020 are medians, while most other countries report means; a few high earners pull the mean up, so medians are usually lower","BMU":"ILOSTAT's figures for 2012–2013 are medians, while most other countries report means; a few high earners pull the mean up, so medians are usually lower","HKG":"ILOSTAT's figures for 2003–2004, 2007, 2009–2016 are medians, while most other countries report means; a few high earners pull the mean up, so medians are usually lower","MAC":"ILOSTAT's figures for 1990–1997, 2009–2018 are medians, while most other countries report means; a few high earners pull the mean up, so medians are usually lower","PAN":"ILOSTAT's figures for 1998–1999 are medians, while most other countries report means; a few high earners pull the mean up, so medians are usually lower","SGP":"ILOSTAT's figures for 2011–2021 are medians, while most other countries report means; a few high earners pull the mean up, so medians are usually lower","UGA":"ILOSTAT's figures for 2002, 2005 are medians, while most other countries report means; a few high earners pull the mean up, so medians are usually lower","TWN":"Taiwan is not in ILOSTAT (it is not an ILO member); average monthly total earnings of employees in industry and services from the DGBAS Earnings and Productivity Survey used instead (annual average, including overtime pay, year-end and performance bonuses; excluding agriculture and public administration), converted at the purchasing power parity for household consumption, the same concept as the World Bank PPP that ILOSTAT uses: from the Penn World Table up to 2021, then carried forward with Taiwan's and US consumer price inflation (NT$14.53 per international dollar in 2025). The IMF's GDP-wide PPP is lower (13.65) and would give Int$4,642. Total earnings were NT$63,383 in 2025, of which regular earnings NT$47,885"},"encoding":"delta","values":{"ABW":[-1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,18604,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"AFG":[-1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,5177,null,null,null,null,null,3186,null,null,null,null,null],"AGO":[-1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,5656,-497,-802,-141,803,-1424,null],"ALB":[-1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,8916,70,294,331,657,126,554,1718,null,null,null],"ARE":[-1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,30173,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,nul